  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale up response against severe acute malnutrition and outbreaks, especially Cholera, in Somali, Oromia and SNNP regions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide quality and integrated health and nutrition assistance to vulnerable people affected by drought. This WHO project provides treatment and consultations for diarrhea and cholera cases, as well as pediatric and malnutrition kits. The project supports 1,082,700 people, including 251,925 women, 242,070 men, 588,705 children, and 190,555 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
